{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1528675-nameless-order-worship-judges","id":1528675,"title":"nameless order/Worship Judges?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-16T14:00:19-08:00","id":1528675,"title":"nameless order/Worship Judges?","content":"Based on this question:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1528646#post1528646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a mage gains the Renowned Artisan merit, what are the strings attached ? Let's say an alchemist wants to learn about the Mesen-Nebu, can they learn through their own research and would that trigger a Judge to target them ? Do they need to believe the Judges are the ultimate arbitrers of Dedwen ? Do they need to keep constantly working for an Arisen cult ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Has anyone written a nameless order/mystery cult based around a Mummy/worshipping the Judges?<br /> <br /> How would it work for awakened mages to attract other to a nameless order where joining meant also being in a Mummy's cult?<br /> <br /> Would a custom legacy be useful for interactions with the Judges (maybe with access to something akin to Exarchal dreams which Prelate's get, but instructions coming from the judges somehow).<br /> <br /> Would it be possible to just earn Mystery Cult Influence in a Mummy's cult without worshipping the Judges? (Or would this be incredibly unwise).<br /> <br /> How would the Pentacle/Seers look at a Nameless order/Awakened cult worshipping these unlikely gods?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-17-2024, 04:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T16:55:13-08:00","id":1528689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1528675-nameless-order-worship-judges#post1528675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would the Pentacle/Seers look at a Nameless order/Awakened cult worshipping these unlikely gods?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the main question I want to answer.<br /> <br /> The Judges are part of a Lower Depth, they lack Sekhem there, so cosmologically? Worshiping those guys is similar to being an Infernalist (Inferno is another Lower Depth with its own set of cultists).<br /> <br /> Of course, depending on how you go about it, it will be more or less restrictive: worshipping ALL Judges is nearly impossible in the modern world, but certain individual Judge credo might be more amenable. Take Arem-Abfu, the Final Judge (Judge of those who commit crimes against reality) it gives a good justification to fight the Abyss, as nothing is more criminal against reality than the Abyss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 01-17-2024, 02:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T06:40:36-08:00","id":1528708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1528675-nameless-order-worship-judges#post1528675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone written a nameless order/mystery cult based around a Mummy/worshipping the Judges?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorta. I once wrote a legacy for an NPC that borrowed the philosophy of the Arisen Alchemists. I don't think I wrote any attainments, it was just a kind of vague outline.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How would it work for awakened mages to attract other to a nameless order where joining meant also being in a Mummy's cult? </div> </div> </div>I suspect it'd be more a case of looking for freshly Awakened mages who don't know any better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would a custom legacy be useful for interactions with the Judges (maybe with access to something akin to Exarchal dreams which Prelate's get, but instructions coming from the judges somehow) </div> </div> </div>I'd use the prelacy mechanics. The Mummy core already uses the paradox mechanics to represent the wrath of the Judges.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would it be possible to just earn Mystery Cult Influence in a Mummy's cult without worshipping the Judges? (Or would this be incredibly unwise). </div> </div> </div>Probably? Like, there are Arisen cults that go rogue and stop worshiping the Judges.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How would the Pentacle/Seers look at a Nameless order/Awakened cult worshipping these unlikely gods? </div> </div> </div>Contact with the Lower Depths is generally a crime under the Lex, whilst the Seers aren't supposed to worship anyone but the Exarchs.<br /> <br /> That said, a lot depends on how you construct your world. Like, how much do Mages know about the Arisen? Even if they don't know details, are they at least a know quantity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T07:00:34-08:00","id":1528709,"title":"","content":"I could see an offshoot of the Sons of Imhotep (the geomancers from the Broken Diamond AP) being interested in the work of the Tef-Aabhi to draw on their knowledge to make more Supernally active locations, or even to engineer just the right configuration to create an Iris back into Imhotep's Emanation Realm. They would provide services in exchange for knowledge of the crafts and use the insights to create novel Attainments.<br /> <br /> Another option would be a Time and Space Legacy focusing on implementing the Great Work of the Judges. Mages are not timeless, but they can be deployed more often and they have enough control of time to be very efficient. Some Attainments could include a <i>Shifting Sands</i> that sends you back up to a scene and uses conjunctional Space to <i>Co-Locate</i> the mage to where they are on the present for the duration, or using a version of <i>Corridors of Time</i> that teleports them where they are on the present, allowing them to maximize what they do in the past. They would look bizarre to the untrained, blinking from place to place in the present and using Istros' Knife to solve issues before they escalate.<br /> <br /> Initiates could be from families that were part of an Arisen cult, promoted to a specialized Nameless Order upon Awakening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T09:10:15-08:00","id":1528717,"title":"","content":"Mummy/Mage crossover material notes that Anpu (the Nameless God) registers very strangely under Mage Sight. He's said to come from the Lower Depths, the Underworld,<i> the Supernal</i> and that even when taken together, these descriptors don't fully explain his nature. If the Judges are anything like him, that leaves individual Mages much more room to argue that messing with Duat should be permissible. There's much more to Obsess about, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T12:35:02-08:00","id":1528736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1528675-nameless-order-worship-judges?p=1528689#post1528689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Worshiping those guys is similar to being an Infernalist (Inferno is another Lower Depth with its own set of cultists).</div> </div> </div> </div>Infernalism isn't really a thing in the Mage lexicon, because there isn't really much impetus to associate with its demonic entities in any capacity, let alone through worship. Like many subjects pertaining to Lower Depths, it's more of an obscure footnote than a cause of great concern.<br /> <br /> I think any question about how other mages respond to a Nameless Order really need to be processed on the level of a single Consilium or even only some of its member cabals, because Nameless Orders are invariably quite small, and this idea of one in particular would seem fairly niche. At that resolution, I would expect mages to have little insight into their philosophy and respond more to any of their actions, good or ill.<br /> <br /> There's a potential hook there for a mage with a particular interest in the ancient Egyptian Great Cult and noticing some of the parallels between that and this Order, if they should have cause to learn more about them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T17:20:20-08:00","id":1528767,"title":"","content":"So maybe an offshoot of the Cwn Annwn (found on page 38 of <i>Left-Handed Path</i>). They could believe that the Judges represent cosmic order, they know Duat is one of the most stable Lower Depths and they can actually make it very difficult for the Exarchs to retgone their domain. So they seize Hallows and other commodities to make Duat more amenable and powerful, with the goal of creating a new great city, one with cosmic oversight against Hubris.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T22:29:41-08:00","id":1528780,"title":"","content":"While mages would categorise Dust as a Lower Depths in terms of how that's their jargon for planes of existence with a seemingly parasitic relationship to native reality that they tend to bundle together, I think it would be something of a shallow relationship for a group of Awakened with a dedicated focus on the place to approach solely in terms of &quot;Lower Depth&quot;, let alone from the direction of &quot;place with no connection whatsoever beyond also being a Lower Depth&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T11:35:30-08:00","id":1528820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500623-ask-a-simple-question-fallen-world-edition?p=1528812#post1528812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With regards to how Mummy metaphysics might interact with Mage ones (a subject I think is prompted when some crossover references go out of their way to describe mage ideas of what the magic of the Shan'iatu was like), I speculate that it's something like... when you look at a place with Mage Sight, the Supernal symbols you can perceive are the lens through which you recognise its meaning, the underlying emotional quality native to it. Sekhem is the actual aspect of the place that provides the basis for those symbols appearing. Any given Awakened may or may not believe that the Supernal and its symbols are the actual origin point of all that, but Sekhem as Mummies recognise and interact with it could probably be seen as its presence in the world as actually experienced. Think of it like how Mage Sight through the Matter Arcanum might tell you many and true things about a crystal of some salt, and you can even cast spells to affect it, but at the end of the day (barring certain philosophical abstractions) the crystal is still a thing that exists for itself rather than just in terms of the symbols it's seen through, and a chemist can have the expertise of that existence to do things with it that are distinct from Supernal magic. I'd say that if a Mummy well versed in their own metaphysics gained a good grounding in mage philosophy, they'd be of the opinion that Sekhem is a quality of the world that precedes any Supernal nature to it, and there can even be mages who would agree with them. Not all sects necessarily regard the relationship of Phenomenal and Supernal in the neo-Platonic terms of &quot;the idealised Forms of which the Supernal is composed are the original template for all phenomena&quot;, and the core book describes some of the ambiguities of their cosmology from which comes a speculation that things might exist first in the Fallen World and then become rarefied to the point of becoming the pure symbols they perceive as transmitting reality (even before getting into the question of influences brought in by strange and alien dimensions).</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes me think of the Free Council, with their focus on human culture and &quot;As Below, So Above&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> Free Council Cabal with their Techn\u00e9 involving the Magical ritual practices of a Mummy cult?<br /> <br /> The use of cults as fairly common practice across the orders makes this seem perfectly reasonable, whether other Mages know that this particular cult has an actual Mummy at its centre or that is a cult secret, is secondary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T03:48:16-08:00","id":1528987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1528675-nameless-order-worship-judges?p=1528820#post1528820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Makes me think of the Free Council, with their focus on human culture and &quot;As Below, So Above&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say it's a perspective on the Supernal that strongly informs and is expressed in the Libertine Creed, but not necessarily 100%. The Free Council has a particular emphasis on human culture there, from both ends; the idea that people as a whole evince the Supernal as it currently exists and that human inspiration creates new Forms. I think there are Diamond philosophies that could easily see the idea of things rising to the Supernal on an individual basis or more inhuman or abstract origin, from which position they assume the occult relationship to the Fallen that they regard most symbols and the foundations of their own Orders to exist in. Helped a bit by the nature of Supernal causality; I think the Free Council sees something of a linear relationship, whereas the Diamond might look upon such additions in terms of creating retroactive shifts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Free Council Cabal with their Techn\u00e9 involving the Magical ritual practices of a Mummy cult?</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly, although that might also depend a bit. I can see a case that being oriented towards Duat makes it insufficiently human cultural for the Supernal Forms the Free Council utilises to really engage with it. It might depend on how much the rituals are expressed in a more recent cultural practice and how much has been cultivated by the Arisen patron to conform to the Law of a Judge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The use of cults as fairly common practice across the orders makes this seem perfectly reasonable, whether other Mages know that this particular cult has an actual Mummy at its centre or that is a cult secret, is secondary.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that Mummy cults tend to be aware of their master/secret weapon even when not calling upon them enough that it would be tricky enough keeping it a secret even from fairly invested regular mages, let alone members. I feel as though in many cases, a cabal of mages is going to have the sort of standing that makes them engage with the Mummy on a level of equal partnership, unless it was one with some particularly nasty powers that ever came right out of the casket swinging in order to enforce a dominance posture that left the sort of impression that lasts even when they're under. Either that or some more subtle, fate binding kind of stuff that more quietly enforces a position of authority.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps some mages who arrive at their own conclusions of subservience to the will of Judges and awe at the nature of the Rite of Return, and defer of their own initiative to an Arisen they view as embodying those things.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T04:01:41-08:00","id":1528988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1528675-nameless-order-worship-judges?p=1528987#post1528987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that Mummy cults tend to be aware of their master/secret weapon even when not calling upon them enough that it would be tricky enough keeping it a secret even from fairly invested regular mages, let alone members. I feel as though in many cases, a cabal of mages is going to have the sort of standing that makes them engage with the Mummy on a level of equal partnership, unless it was one with some particularly nasty powers that ever came right out of the casket swinging in order to enforce a dominance posture that left the sort of impression that lasts even when they're under. Either that or some more subtle, fate binding kind of stuff that more quietly enforces a position of authority.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I meant secret from those other mages who might decide the cabal was being left-handed.<br /> <br /> I assume all cult members and even mages who may only have the cult influence merit, would know.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or perhaps some mages who arrive at their own conclusions of subservience to the will of Judges and awe at the nature of the Rite of Return, and defer of their own initiative to an Arisen they view as embodying those things. </div> </div> </div>That seems reasonable, of course I could imagine a Mummy cult which either has one of its members awaken, or a newly awakened mages joining a cult before they meet with other mages (like wanting to find out more about magic and finding this esoteric cult first .. or being annoyed by the Pentacle orders approach because they don't like being told what to do and joining a mummy cult instead).<br /> <br /> Either case they could end up by default ina subservient position without necessarily knowing all the details of the cult in advance.<br /> <br /> But the Free Council / Human culture question intrigued m\u00e9<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Possibly, although that might also depend a bit. I can see a case that being oriented towards Duat makes it insufficiently human cultural for the Supernal Forms the Free Council utilises to really engage with it. </div> </div> </div>Does being aligned to Duat mean there is no Supernal reflection of the practices? This is interesting to me, I guess if that is the case it would apply to lower Depths in general (how the Strix/Dis or the Luciferge/Inferno interact with mages/the Supernal).<br /> <br /> I kinda considered Iremite culture to be part of sleeper culture until you suggested this. But i am happy to hear another take!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T08:08:12-08:00","id":1529007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1528675-nameless-order-worship-judges?p=1528988#post1528988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I meant secret from those other mages who might decide the cabal was being left-handed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've yet to look at Contagion Chronicle stuff myself, but between that, some of the Dark Ages stuff, and even a couple of points in the likes of Signs of Sorcery, I think there's a reasonable case for Pentacle society to make some accommodations for the idea of mages who have intertwined themselves a bit with other supernaturals. Perhaps looked askance at a bit, but not necessarily accused of committing some crime or profanity against magic as a matter of course.<br /> <br /> Although the other side of that is my being personally inclined to assume that most cabals in a Consilium are pretty secretive from one another as a matter of course, even when they're all being perfectly orthodox. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems reasonable, of course I could imagine a Mummy cult which either has one of its members awaken, or a newly awakened mages joining a cult before they meet with other mages (like wanting to find out more about magic and finding this esoteric cult first .. or being annoyed by the Pentacle orders approach because they don't like being told what to do and joining a mummy cult instead).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't quite think that Mummy cults present very many avenues for entry to people who don't already possess some basis for being sponsored in. Like, if the cult is in the backbone of some corporation, they're mostly drawing in people who work for the corporation and can become personally associated with existing members. That being in cases where they don't outright form a community that brings people up from birth for membership. <br /> <br /> A new mage might have the sensory powers to discern something surrounding the group that seems worth following up on and presenting themselves with questions, but I think in a lot of cases the cultists are going to respond to that with suspicion and fear, even if the mage doesn't actively introduce themselves as having powers. Some follow up investigation to figure out how this stranger has sussed them out. If the mage can employ powers to thwart such methods, that just becomes more suspicious, and might even escalate to waking the Arisen.<br /> <br /> A sufficiently devious new mage might seek to infiltrate in more organic fashion, like joining the company in the usual manner and putting the desirable qualities in the line of sight of recruiters until they work their way in, but I think understanding of such methods will be uncommon across regular new Awakened. Even then, it ends up as a rather dedicated strategy for somebody who's supposed to be unsure of what they're looking for.<br /> <br /> Awakening from within the cult is not impossible, but I'd say there's a question of whether or not cult activities might interfere. Not even just in terms of what they mean for the person's supernatural familiarity that affects shocking confrontations with the Lie, but just... time to themselves. The kind of Awakening that doesn't take place totally within your mind tends to entail going about conducting some activity that you really need to be alone for, so that you can carry them to their conclusion without interruption.<br /> <br /> Hmm, I've seen people express scepticism about how many newly Awakened are supposed to embrace the Orders, and it occurs to me that an unspoken assumption of Awakening is that it might occur to people who are already a bit alienated from others. Otherwise, they might have people in their lives who would interfere when they start behaving very strangely, and possibly shake them out of the state of Lucidity.<br /> <br /> As for being told what to do, the Diamond Orders have fairly flat hierarchies and aren't really much about being commanding towards any of their members who aren't actively presenting themselves for such, and even then there's always the option of the Free Council (which presumably gets taken at the rate that makes it the largest Order).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either case they could end up by default ina subservient position without necessarily knowing all the details of the cult in advance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, but the relationship between cult and Mummy can be complicated, more circular than just the Arisen being the one in command. They're at the centre and are a figure of reverence, but at the same time the cult will be educated in the rites that will resurrect the Mummy and endow it with purpose, that the raised being will be strongly inclined towards carrying out. These are often purposes that are directly beneficial to the cult. When that's not going on, the Mummy is often completely absent. Either way, not entirely a situation where membership puts you under the Arisen's thumb.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does being aligned to Duat mean there is no Supernal reflection of the practices? This is interesting to me, I guess if that is the case it would apply to lower Depths in general (how the Strix/Dis or the Luciferge/Inferno interact with mages/the Supernal).</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily without Supernal connection as not the correct kinds of Supernal connection for Free Council knowledge to harness as a Yantra like that. It's like with any Order tool; masks clearly have a reflection, but Arrows can't use them the way Guardians can.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda considered Iremite culture to be part of sleeper culture until you suggested this. But i am happy to hear another take!</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that Irem isn't just realistic proto-dynastic Egypt that happened to be aware of deities in Irem. The Nameless Empire was founded and ruled by inhuman beings sent as emissaries by the Judges (and possibly higher gods than them, I'm not fully familiar with the lore) in what is implied or stated to be somewhere between the expression of some mysterious cosmic intrigue and a project of deliberately founding a society to serve as a mechanism for channelling Sekhem into Duat. My crude understanding of how the latter works is basically along the lines of &quot;make a society subject to the law of the Judges, so that when its people inevitably break them, the Judges will have authority to condemn them to the Devourer (keeping her satisfied enough to remain at bay and not consume everything)&quot;.<br /> <br /> Plus some other stuff, Mummy lore runs deep and goes to some unsettling and difficult to parse places. The basic point stands that it wasn't just a normal human culture, even if it's supposed to provide a template that many other human cultures followed.<br /> <br /> That's before getting into stuff like how the inhuman entities attempted to harness its resources to rebel against their masters and elevate themselves to the level of gods, by means of sacrificing the entire population and even kind of breaking Irem's place in history (which is why Tome of the Pentacle described it as a closed uchronia). That's where Mummies actually come from, somewhere between a lynchpin in that great mystical working and the means by which the Judges sabotaged and co-opted it to provide themselves with more reliable emissaries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T12:59:56-08:00","id":1529034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1528675-nameless-order-worship-judges?p=1529007#post1529007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&lt;Snip&gt;<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that Irem isn't just realistic proto-dynastic Egypt that happened to be aware of deities in Irem. The Nameless Empire was founded and ruled by inhuman beings sent as emissaries by the Judges (and possibly higher gods than them, I'm not fully familiar with the lore) in what is implied or stated to be somewhere between the expression of some mysterious cosmic intrigue and a project of deliberately founding a society to serve as a mechanism for channelling Sekhem into Duat. My crude understanding of how the latter works is basically along the lines of &quot;make a society subject to the law of the Judges, so that when its people inevitably break them, the Judges will have authority to condemn them to the Devourer (keeping her satisfied enough to remain at bay and not consume everything)&quot;.<br /> <br /> Plus some other stuff, Mummy lore runs deep and goes to some unsettling and difficult to parse places. The basic point stands that it wasn't just a normal human culture, even if it's supposed to provide a template that many other human cultures followed.<br /> <br /> That's before getting into stuff like how the inhuman entities attempted to harness its resources to rebel against their masters and elevate themselves to the level of gods, by means of sacrificing the entire population and even kind of breaking Irem's place in history (which is why Tome of the Pentacle described it as a closed uchronia). That's where Mummies actually come from, somewhere between a lynchpin in that great mystical working and the means by which the Judges sabotaged and co-opted it to provide themselves with more reliable emissaries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so not so much 'this isn't supernal' more this isn't typical 'sleeper' culture. Hmm.<br /> <br /> I think a Godly inspired culture created by humans is still Human culture in some sense at least to the point where the Free Councillors in question could find some of their practices sufficiently resonant.<br /> <br /> Like I probably wouldn't include Wolf/Pack Rites from WtF as a techn\u00e9, but I would include Necromancy from Geist. You have to draw the line somewhere...<br /> <br /> Anyway, thank you for the very informative and interesting discussion. I think I would not have a Strix lead/Patroned Cult qualify, and I don't know enough about the Luciferge (sp?) May even get around to reading Inferno and/or Hunter at some point... (If I ever finish Promethean, Lost, Demon and Mummy)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T13:08:34-08:00","id":1529035,"title":"","content":"On the mages in a Mummy Cult, I think someone born into the cult, who later awakens, and then learns about Mage society (from other mages trying to recruit) and thus forms a cabal/nameless order dedicated to investigating the Mummy, Judges, Duat etc. Recruiting other mages, offering them rare magic items and insights into where to find more (cult knowledge) while actually inducting them into the cult (or telling the rest of the cult that is what they are doing)... Would definitely make for some interesting cross-over potential.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}